From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:48:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 471/488] [DS4.1] TileLang declares no B12X preparation unit

Under the TileLang kernel family the attention helpers declared a B12X
rotary plan (kept for the attention staging it allocated) and cache-writer
plans, and every compressor built a B12X grouped-RMSNorm plan; serving
launched none of them. The helpers now declare nothing under TileLang,
the layer's kernel binding allocates the same staging before memory
profiling, cache writes look up a B12X plan only under B12X, and the
compressor's norm holds just its weight. The B12X family is unchanged.
